# The benchmark's pinned datasets are checksummed inputs. Without an explicit
# entry git leaves their line endings to the platform, so the same commit gives
# a Windows checkout CRLF and a Linux one LF, and a hash taken over the bytes
# rejects the file on the other machine while the rows are identical.
#
# Two mechanisms, deliberately agreeing rather than one covering for the other:
# this pins the working tree to LF everywhere, and `run_benchmark.py`
# normalises line endings before hashing, so verification holds even in a
# checkout that predates this file.
benchmark/data/*.csv text eol=lf
benchmark/results.csv text eol=lf

# Preserved run evidence is what a run actually printed. Git must not rewrite
# it in either direction, so it is marked as not-text rather than pinned to a
# line ending: an evidence file that changes on checkout is not evidence.
benchmark/runs/**/stdout.txt -text
benchmark/runs/**/stderr.txt -text
